  "html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Transitional//EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-transitional.dtd"><html dir="ltr" lang="en"><head><meta content="text/html; charset=UTF-8" http-equiv="Content-Type"/><meta name="x-apple-disable-message-reformatting"/><meta name="color-scheme" content="light only"/><meta name="supported-color-schemes" content="light only"/><title>About Tuesday’s vote on the park fee</title><style>:root{color-scheme:light only;supported-color-schemes:light only}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){.em-bg{background-color:#DDF2E8 !important}.em-card{background-color:#FFFFFF !important}.em-header{background-color:#16695C !important}.em-rule{background-color:#16695C !important}.em-band{background-color:#16695C !important}.em-divider{background-color:#B2E1CC !important}.em-accent{background-color:#FFE06C !important}.em-cta{background-color:#257F68 !important}.em-header-text{color:#FFFFFF !important}.em-headline{color:#043630 !important}.em-subheading{color:#16695C !important}.em-body{color:#115449 !important}.em-meta{color:#115449 !important}.em-cta-text{color:#FFFFFF !important}.em-cta-link{color:#257F68 !important}.em-accent-text{color:#043630 !important}}@media only screen and (max-width:620px){.em-pad{padding-left:20px !important;padding-right:20px !important}.em-page{padding-left:0 !important;padding-right:0 !important}}</style></head><body bgcolor="#FFFFFF" class="em-card" style="background-color:#FFFFFF;margin:0;padding:0"><!--$--><!--html--><!--head--><!--body--><table border="0" width="100%" cellPadding="0" cellSpacing="0" role="presentation" align="center"><tbody><tr><td style="margin:0;padding:0;background-color:#FFFFFF;font-family:-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &#x27;Segoe UI&#x27;, Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellPadding="0" cellSpacing="0" border="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" class="em-card" style="background-color:#FFFFFF;width:100%"><tbody><tr><td align="left" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" class="em-card em-page" style="background-color:#FFFFFF;padding:24px 12px;text-align:left"><table role="presentation" width="600" cellPadding="0" cellSpacing="0" border="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" class="em-card" style="width:100%;max-width:600px;background-color:#FFFFFF;margin:0 auto"><tbody><tr><td style="padding:0"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellPadding="0" cellSpacing="0" border="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" class="em-card" style="background-color:#FFFFFF;width:100%"><tbody><tr><td align="left" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" class="em-card em-pad" style="background-color:#FFFFFF;padding:32px 32px 16px;text-align:left"><p class="em-body" style="font-size:16px;line-height:26px;margin:0 0 16px;color:#115449;text-align:left;margin-top:0;margin-right:0;margin-bottom:16px;margin-left:0"><span>Dear {{first_name}},</span></p><p class="em-body" style="font-size:16px;line-height:26px;margin:0 0 16px;color:#115449;text-align:left;margin-top:0;margin-right:0;margin-bottom:16px;margin-left:0"><span>On Tuesday the board voted 4 to 1 to add a $2 parking fee at Lakeside Park on weekends. I was the one no vote, and I want you to hear why from me.</span></p><p class="em-body" style="font-size:16px;line-height:26px;margin:0 0 16px;color:#115449;text-align:left;margin-top:0;margin-right:0;margin-bottom:16px;margin-left:0"><span>The fee covers about a third of the park’s repair backlog. I agree the repairs can’t wait. But families who use the park most told me $2 every weekend adds up, and I think we can close the gap with the state grant we applied for in August.</span></p><p class="em-body" style="font-size:16px;line-height:26px;margin:0 0 16px;color:#115449;text-align:left;margin-top:0;margin-right:0;margin-bottom:16px;margin-left:0"><span>The fee is up for review in six months. Before then, I’d like to know what you think.</span></p><p class="em-body" style="font-size:16px;line-height:26px;margin:0 0 16px;color:#115449;text-align:left;margin-top:0;margin-right:0;margin-bottom:16px;margin-left:0"><span>The fee starts Saturday, November 7, and the board will review it at the May meeting.</span></p><p class="em-body" style="font-size:16px;line-height:26px;margin:0 0 16px;color:#115449;text-align:left;margin-top:0;margin-right:0;margin-bottom:16px;margin-left:0"><span>Thank you,<br/></span><span>Priya Natarajan<br/></span><span>Township Trustee</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellPadding="0" cellSpacing="0" border="0" bgcolor="#B2E1CC" class="em-divider" style="background-color:#B2E1CC;width:100%"><tbody><tr><td align="left" bgcolor="#B2E1CC" class="em-divider" height="1" style="background-color:#B2E1CC;padding:0;text-align:left;height:1px;line-height:1px;font-size:1px"> </td></tr></tbody></table><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellPadding="0" cellSpacing="0" border="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" class="em-card" style="background-color:#FFFFFF;width:100%"><tbody><tr><td align="left" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" class="em-card em-pad" style="background-color:#FFFFFF;padding:24px 32px 32px;text-align:left"><p class="em-meta" style="font-size:13px;line-height:20px;margin:0 0 8px;color:#115449;text-align:left;margin-top:0;margin-right:0;margin-bottom:8px;margin-left:0">Paid for by Wells for Mayor</p><p class="em-meta" style="font-size:13px;line-height:20px;margin:0 0 8px;color:#115449;text-align:left;margin-top:0;margin-right:0;margin-bottom:8px;margin-left:0">You’re getting this email because you asked to hear from Renee Wells.</p><p class="em-meta" style="font-size:13px;line-height:20px;margin:0 0 8px;color:#115449;text-align:left;margin-top:0;margin-right:0;margin-bottom:8px;margin-left:0">916 Silver Spur Rd #310, Rolling Hills Estates, CA 90274</p><p class="em-meta" style="font-size:13px;line-height:20px;margin:0;color:#115449;text-align:left;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0"><a href="{{unsubscribe_url}}" ses:no-track="" class="em-meta" style="color:#115449;text-decoration-line:none;text-decoration:underline" target="_blank">Unsubscribe</a></p></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table><!--/$--></body></html>",
  "subject": "About Tuesday’s vote on the park fee",
  "text": "Dear {{first_name}},

On Tuesday the board voted 4 to 1 to add a $2 parking fee at Lakeside Park on weekends. I was the one no vote, and I want you to hear why from me.

The fee covers about a third of the park’s repair backlog. I agree the repairs can’t wait. But families who use the park most told me $2 every weekend adds up, and I think we can close the gap with the state grant we applied for in August.

The fee is up for review in six months. Before then, I’d like to know what you think.

The fee starts Saturday, November 7, and the board will review it at the May meeting.

Thank you,
Priya Natarajan
Township Trustee

 

Paid for by Wells for Mayor

You’re getting this email because you asked to hear from Renee Wells.

916 Silver Spur Rd #310, Rolling Hills Estates, CA 90274

Unsubscribe {{unsubscribe_url}}",
}
`;

